 "lines": [
  "The wall of their plane just blew out.",
  "Sunday after Thanksgiving, the busiest day of the year to fly.",
  "Kai, Mia and Leo are flying home at thirty-five thousand feet.",
  "Then, a bang. A panel [tears](tairz) off the side of the plane.",
  "Air rushes out. Fog fills the cabin, and it turns freezing cold.",
  "Outside, it's about minus sixty-five degrees. Way colder than your freezer.",
  "The air's so thin, you'd have thirty seconds to a [minute](minnit) before you can't think straight.",
  "@am_echo: \"Mia! Let me help you first!\"",
  "@af_heart: \"No! Your mask first, Leo!\"",
  "She's right. Help others first, and you could pass out before you finish.",
  "Pull the mask down to start the oxygen. The bag may not inflate, but it works.",
  "Those masks hold at least ten [minutes](minnits) of oxygen. That's enough.",
  "The pilots are already diving to ten thousand feet, where you can breathe.",
  "@am_michael: \"Stay buckled! Stuff's flying out that hole!\"",
  "Here's the twist. This really happened.",
  "January twenty twenty-four. Alaska Airlines Flight twelve eighty-two, just out of Portland.",
  "At almost fifteen thousand feet, a plug over an unused exit blew off.",
  "The two seats next to the hole were empty. Nobody died.",
  "Investigators found the four bolts meant to hold it in place were missing.",
  "And one phone fell almost three miles, landed under a bush, and still worked.",
  "So stay buckled, even when the sign is off. Because sometimes,"
